.TH QUANUX-SOVEREIGN 1 "FEBRUARY 2026" "QuanuX Institutional" "QuanuX Manual Pages"
.SH NAME
quanux-sentinel \- Hardware-Enforced Risk Management Gate
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quanux-sentinel
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B quanux-sentinel
daemon represents the "Adult in the Room" for the QuanuX Distributed Execution framework. Running strictly as a bare-metal C++ loop on an isolated core (ordinarily Core 5), the Sentinel possesses unilateral authority over the L3 Cache \fBSovereignState\fR.

It enforces the fundamental risk guardrails of the trading strategy without relying on context switches or syscall routing, avoiding de-scheduling jitter.

.SH PRIVILEGE SEPARATION
The architecture demands absolute Process Isolation:
.TP
.BR quanux-sentinel
An independent binary explicitly bound to Core 5. It holds absolute ownership of the `risk_interlock` and the Master Kill Switch.
.TP
.BR quanux-spreader
The primary execution engine bound to Core 3. It "leases" execution permissions from the Sentinel across the L3 Cache `SovereignState` memory. 

If the \fBquanux-sentinel\fR process is terminated, or heartbeat drift exceeds 1ms, the \fBquanux-spreader\fR is compelled to enter \fBSTATE_HALT\fR immediately.
.SH THE NATURAL LAWS (RISK RULES)
The Sentinel enforces the QuanuX Natural Laws via the following "Sin" checks:
.TP
.BR Stale\ Tick\ (Drift)
Monitors the `tsc_lo` heartbeat. If the delta exceeds 3,000,000 cycles (~1ms at 3GHz), the Spreader's data is stale. The Sentinel issues an immediate HALT.
.TP
.BR Notional\ Breach
Calculates: `abs_pos * tap.best_bid`. If the result breaches the hard-coded absolute threshold (e.g., $5M limit), the Sentinel drops the interlock constraint.
.TP
.BR Order\ Storm
Tracks `orders_fired` byte. If it climbs faster than the allocated burst per physical second, the interlock closes the flood gates.
.TP
.BR Partial\ Fills\ (Ruthless but Safe)
If `ExecutionState::PARTIAL` is registered, the Sentinel limits scaling. It replaces the `max_position_limit_` with the exactly executed current quantity dynamically, permitting hedging exits but halting further toxic accumulations.
.SH ASSEMBLY INSTRUCTIONS
The HALT is enacted utilizing the \fBLOCK BTS\fR (Bit Test and Set) assembly instruction.
Instead of an expensive `std::atomic` exchange cache flush, `LOCK BTS` physically flips the 0th bit of the risk_interlock byte.
Execution cycle impact on Core 5: ~18-35 CPU cycles.
Spreader awareness delay on Core 3: ~59 CPU nanoseconds (L3 Cache bus synchronization latency).
.SH ISOLATION
The Sentinel is expressly forbidden from triggering \fBstd::cout\fR or interacting with the OS scheduler.
.SH THE THEATER OF THE MIND
(The Ritchie Protocol Override)

This system was not built. It was performed. The 11.33ns halt is not an optimization; it is the climax of the first act. Ensure that all future logic updates maintain the purity of the Performance.
